<item><title>Russian House chief Dimitri Sytyi claims ignorance of Ndassima gold revenue</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/russian-house-chief-dimitri-sytyi-claims-ignorance-of-1d256a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/russian-house-chief-dimitri-sytyi-claims-ignorance-of-1d256a/</guid><category>Central African Republic</category><description>Sytyi said on Radio Ndeke Luka on 22 September 2026 that mercenary presence in the Central African Republic was free of charge.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:00:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cf.jpg" length="41097" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cf.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Central African justice minister orders prosecution of BRDC</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/central-african-justice-minister-orders-prosecution-of-brdc-f6a131/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/central-african-justice-minister-orders-prosecution-of-brdc-f6a131/</guid><category>Central African Republic</category><description>The ministry says the political platform is absent from official party registers and has no authorisation after its 13 November march.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:35:51 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/central-african-justice-minister-orders-prosecution-of-brdc-f6a131/share.jpg" length="41604" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/central-african-justice-minister-orders-prosecution-of-brdc-f6a131/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Former Central African Republic prime minister Nicolas Tiangaye dies at 70</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/former-central-african-republic-prime-minister-nicolas-c7deec/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/former-central-african-republic-prime-minister-nicolas-c7deec/</guid><category>Central African Republic</category><description>The lawyer and opposition figure died in Bangui on 16 November after a sudden illness, leaving a decades-long record in law and politics.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:17:18 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cf.jpg" length="41097" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cf.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
