<item><title>ANAC equips Bangui-M’Poko airport and trains more than 70 staff</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/anac-equips-bangui-m-poko-airport-and-trains-more-than-70-4b1956/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/anac-equips-bangui-m-poko-airport-and-trains-more-than-70-4b1956/</guid><category>Central African Republic</category><description>The Central African aviation authority handed out certificates and security equipment at the airport on Thursday 12 November, with funding from the African Development Bank.</description><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:17:41 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cf.jpg" length="41097" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cf.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
